#1241","p":50,"im":["93e4c82b7ca5d468f25f5b5203301319321325b1"],"m":1241},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1242","t":"","a":"JB888","d":"","n":"#1242","p":50,"im":["c3d9bbc4317e335d1bea5f29003b940b985242f7"],"m":1242},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1243","t":"HI m new to this PA n posting a chart of usd/chf M1 in the last minutes of market on friday... i hv asked sm queries kindly reply me as i dnt knw anything n want to learn PA properly... n please leave ur suggestions n if i hv made any mistakes kindly lemme know so that i can improve upon them...\n\nregards\n\nnys","a":"nysforex","d":"","n":"#1243","p":50,"im":["0c53cce97365f88b96fcfe1319c1cc6f2d5dcfc2"],"m":1243},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1244","t":"pin bar is more like this\n\nCharacteristics of the Pin Bar Formation\n\n• The pin bar should have a long upper or lower tail…the tail is also sometimes called the “wick” or the “shadow”…they all mean the same thing. It’s the “pointy” part of the pin bar that literally looks like a “tail” and that shows rejection or false break of a level.\n\n• The area between the open and close of the pin bar is called the “body” or “real body”. It is typically colored white or another light color when the close was higher than the open and black or another dark color when the close was lower than the open.\n\n• The open and close of the pin bar should be very close together or equal (same price), the closer the better.\n\n• The open and close of the pin bar are near one end of the bar, the closer to the end the better.\n\n• The shadow or tail of the pin bar sticks out (protrudes) from the surrounding price bars, the longer the tail of the pin bar the better.\n\n• A general “rule of thumb” is that you want to see the pin bar tail be two/thirds the total pin bar length or more and the rest of the pin bar should be one/third the total pin bar length or less.\n\n• The end opposite the tail is sometimes referred to as the “nose”","a":"roqallo","d":"","n":"#1244","p":50,"im":["d4a8f4418e81f3e418be50e900866399c1f3e48a"],"m":1244},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1245","t":"thx roqallo for enlightening me about pin bars n ur kind reply...will take care of all this stuff from now on...","a":"nysforex","d":"","n":"#1245","p":50,"im":[],"m":1245},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1246","t":"","a":"JB888","d":"","n":"#1246","p":50,"im":["a2b7d5e1f4a8c47310626612c29112affcbbe0e2"],"m":1246},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1247","t":"","a":"JB888","d":"","n":"#1247","p":50,"im":["c2fd425da143d35d24a189d702eab631118c3abf"],"m":1247},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1248","t":"","a":"JB888","d":"","n":"#1248","p":50,"im":["f2657204e43b34a1f91cf1739971dd00d43efbd4","ee8ee6d616cb5b1ca9b7e94e3d34e553c1bf024b"],"m":1248},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1249","t":"nysforex wrote: HI m new to this PA n posting a chart of usd/chf M1 in the last minutes of market on friday... i hv asked sm queries kindly reply me as i dnt knw anything n want to learn PA properly... n please leave ur suggestions n if i hv made any mistakes kindly lemme know so that i can improve upon them...\n\nregards nys\n\nHi Here at RTM we dont trade pin bars, inside bars etc, I think i read somewhere IF said that closing of bar have no significance when placing a trade. We trade areas instead, and figuring out where these areas are is what we try to learn.","a":"TheLastNail","d":"","n":"#1249","p":50,"im":["0c53cce97365f88b96fcfe1319c1cc6f2d5dcfc2"],"m":1249},{"id":"dbrrbd_p50_1250","t":"454647484950515253","a":"JB888","d":"","n":"#1250","p":50,"im":["eb959ee100095f13a682d8ebb6e35a0ff224f069","971ef7d16f82a04ac3a99fc6c3e3717bf9080672"],"m":1250}],"images":[{"k":"a0524f803833423cccbede0330e0bfc8443520af","t":"assets/thumbs/a0524f803833423cccbede0330e0bfc8443520af.webp","f":"assets/images/a0524f803833423cccbede0330e0bfc8443520af.png","w":1366,"h":628,"b":22837,"o":"a0524f803833423cccbede0330e0bfc8443520af.png","p":50,"pid":"dbrrbd_p50_1226"},{"k":"9ac27a2e19a773d1461fe42dea3b54b26d11e490","t":"assets/thumbs/9ac27a2e19a773d1461fe42dea3b54b26d11e490.webp","f":"assets/images/9ac27a2e19a773d1461fe42dea3b54b